66. Safety Intervention Hierarchy

When an unsafe trajectory is identified, possible intervention levels include:
1. Information
2. Permission
3. Authority
4. Capability
5. Coupling
6. Oversight
7. DOS
8. Environment
9. Action
10. Configuration
11. Trajectory
The safest intervention point is not necessarily the lowest-level intervention.

The appropriate intervention depends on:

* severity;
* timing;
* reversibility;
* authority;
* uncertainty;
* affected entities;
* feasibility.

