74. Falsification Conditions

The Entity DOS hypothesis should remain falsifiable.

Evidence against the operational value of DOS would include:

* no measurable behavioural improvement;
* no improvement over simpler policies;
* no improvement in authority management;
* no improvement in trajectory detection;
* excessive computational cost;
* excessive human oversight burden;
* inability to generalize;
* equivalent performance from existing approaches;
* increased false positives;
* increased operational complexity without corresponding safety benefit.

If evidence shows that DOS provides no meaningful advantage, the framework should be modified or abandoned in its current form.

