Entity Dynamic Operational Specification (Entity DOS):

A dynamic analytical and operational representation of an entity’s purpose, role, responsibilities, capabilities, authority, permissions, information, constraints, affected entities, environmental conditions, oversight, uncertainty and trajectory conditions, together with the conditions under which that specification may change as the surrounding configuration changes.

